      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    loan_amount = 300000\n    loan_term_years = 30\n    original_rate = 0.045\n    new_rate = 0.04\n    float_down_fee_percent = 0.4\n\n    # Calculate monthly interest rates and total number of payments\n    original_monthly_rate = original_rate / 12\n    new_monthly_rate = new_rate / 12\n    total_payments = loan_term_years * 12\n\n    # Calculate monthly mortgage payments\n    original_payment = (\n        loan_amount * original_monthly_rate\n        / (1 - (1 + original_monthly_rate) ** -total_payments)\n    )\n    new_payment = (\n        loan_amount * new_monthly_rate\n        / (1 - (1 + new_monthly_rate) ** -total_payments)\n    )\n\n    # Calculate total payment savings and subtract the float down fee\n    total_payment_savings = (original_payment - new_payment) * total_payments\n    float_down_fee = loan_amount * (float_down_fee_percent / 100)\n    net_savings = total_payment_savings - float_down_fee\n\n    # Return savings rounded to the nearest dollar\n    return round(net_savings)\n```",
